ny hands my opponent could reasonably have. Given that I'm ahead in the overall game and have 4 hands remaining, I should avoid marginal situations.\n\nReason: I have middle pair with a weak kicker (10s with 5), facing a significant raise on the flop. My opponent's 1663 raise suggests strength - likely top pair (Queens) or better. With no draws and being out of position against aggression, continuing would be speculatively expensive. Since I'm ahead by 10,400 chips overall with 4 hands remaining, I should avoid marginal spots and preserve my lead. Folding is the disciplined play here.\n\nAnswer: -1"}
